title: $:/core/Hosting

/*\
This tiddler documents the protocol used by the `postmessage` saver to host
a single-file TiddlyWiki inside an iframe belonging to another web page.
\*/

! Hosting TiddlyWiki in an iframe

A host page can embed a single-file TiddlyWiki in an iframe and take responsibility for saving it, and for keeping its own UI in step with the wiki's page title and favicon. Communication uses `window.postMessage` together with `MessageChannel`/`MessagePort`, so that each subscription gets its own dedicated port.

!! Subscribing

To subscribe to a topic, the host creates a `MessageChannel` and posts a subscription message to the iframe's window, transferring one end of the channel:

```
var channel = new MessageChannel();
iframe.contentWindow.postMessage({verb: "SUBSCRIBE", to: topic}, targetOrigin, [channel.port2]);
```

`topic` is one of:

|!Topic |!Meaning
|`SAVE` |The host wants to receive the complete wiki HTML whenever the wiki is saved
|`PAGETITLE` |The host wants the wiki's page title
|`FAVICON` |The host wants the wiki's favicon as a data URI

Each subscription is independent: a port receives messages only for the topic named in its subscription. As soon as a subscription is accepted the current value of the topic (if any) is sent immediately, so the host does not have to wait for the next change.

!! Saving

When the wiki is saved manually or auto-saved, each port subscribed to `SAVE` receives:

```
{verb: "SAVE", method: "save" | "autosave", body: "<full wiki HTML>"}
```

The host must reply on the same port with:

```
{verb: "OK"}
```

to confirm that the save succeeded. Any other reply verb (optionally with a `reason` string) is treated as an error and shown to the user; the wiki remains dirty so that the save can be retried. If no reply arrives within the timeout (default 10 seconds, configurable via the tiddler `$:/config/PostMessageSaver/Timeout`), the save is reported as failed.

While at least one host is subscribed to `SAVE`, the `postmessage` saver handles all saves; when no host is subscribed (or all hosts have unsubscribed), saving falls through to the other installed savers such as the download saver.

!! Page title and favicon

Ports subscribed to `PAGETITLE` receive `{verb: "PAGETITLE", body: <title string>}` whenever the wiki's page title changes, and ports subscribed to `FAVICON` receive `{verb: "FAVICON", body: <data URI or null>}` whenever the favicon tiddler changes.

!! Unsubscribing

A host can stop receiving a topic by posting on its own port:

```
channel.port1.postMessage({verb: "UNSUBSCRIBE", to: topic});
```

Closing the port entirely has the same effect: subsequent saves then fall through to other savers.
